# 📜 Architecture Decision Records & Spec-Drift Sentinel (`sdlc-adr`)

## 1. When to Use `/sdlc-adr`

Per **`INV-03`**, any PR that modifies `PRODUCT.md`, `docs/specs/*.md`, dependency manifests (`package.json`, `pom.xml`, `pyproject.toml`, `go.mod`, `Cargo.toml`), database migrations, C4 architecture diagrams, or OpenAPI/GraphQL contracts must be backed by an accepted ADR in `docs/adr/ADR-00X-*.md`.

---

## 2. ADR Lifecycle Commands

```bash
# 1. Check for undeclared spec, dependency, schema, or contract drift
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs drift check

# 2. Mint a new ADR (technical/architectural scope auto-accepts; product/contract scope pauses for human approval)
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs adr create \
  --title "<Decision Title>" \
  --scope <technical|architectural|product|contract> \
  --ticket <id> \
  --supersedes "<CAP-XX>" \
  --context "<Why this change is needed>" \
  --decision "<Chosen architectural approach>" \
  --consequences "<Downstream impact & trade-offs>"

# 3. List all ADRs and their approval status
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs adr list

# 4. Approve or reject a pending product/contract ADR
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs adr decide --id ADR-00X --status <accepted|rejected> --by "@lead"

# 5. Compact accepted ADRs into docs/SRS.md and reset PRODUCT.md ADR index (baseline or release cut)
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs adr compact --release <version> [--dry-run]

# 6. Synchronize the Causal Decision Graph (docs/DECISION_MAP.md) & Architecture UI
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs decision-graph sync
node .agent/scripts/sdlc-engine.mjs ui-snapshot
```
